GATE 2 — VERDICT.

Evidence directory: {{ .run_dir }}/evidence
Start with summary.md, then read report.md, plan.md, refs.md, and
each run-<label>.md.

Reproduction results (authoritative — these are the subworkflow's
own reported outcomes; if summary.md disagrees with them, these win
and you must say so in your reason):
  main   ({{ .main_sha }}): {{ .repro_main }}
  stable ({{ .stable_tag }}): {{ .repro_stable }}

Design-intent file (empty if none supplied): {{ .design_intent_file }}
When a path is given, read it BEFORE applying test 4. Behavior it
records as intended is not a defect, however strong the reproduction.

Apply the verdict matrix and the four evidence tests from your
instructions. Judge only what the evidence shows.

Test 4 is the one this workflow most often gets wrong. Existing
implementation and passing tests establish current behavior, not
intent. Escalate only when authoritative user-visible contracts
conflict or the report does not state required observable behavior.

Call submit_outcome with `reproduced`, `regression`, `already_fixed`,
`not_reproduced`, `insufficient_evidence`, or `needs_human`.